         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "Think about it: when we count 1, 2, 3... each number is exactly 1 more than the one before. Can we say that counting is the same as adding 1 each time?",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "06f7e8d9-1a0b-4f2c-3d4e-5f6a7b8c9d0e",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "yes",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "06f7e8d9-1a0b-4f2c-3d4e-5f6a7b8c9d0e",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "party",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "1ae03186-6cd0-451d-ae10-d5107cbe9651",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=1ae03186-6cd0-451d-ae10-d5107cbe9651",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nNow we see the secret behind counting: it is just addition in disguise! Every time we count, we add 1 to get to the next number:\n\n0 + 1 = 1\n1 + 1 = 2\n2 + 1 = 3\n3 + 1 = 4\n4 + 1 = 5\n5 + 1 = 6\n6 + 1 = 7\n7 + 1 = 8\n8 + 1 = 9\n\nLike learning to walk, we have taken our first steps in understanding how numbers connect. Each +1 is a small step forward. In the next class, we will explore what happens when we reach 9 and need to take one more step!",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
